# The sibling of a-guess-that-only-one-way-through-a-turn-leans-on-is-not-asked-in-front-of-the-loop.ir, for lists. `extra` is undefined in the first call and no turn of it reads `extra[i]`. Asked in front,
# "is it an array" failed and all turns ran in the other copy: three times the instructions. It came there by two roads: findListsReadInLoop() listed every list that any block of the loop reads, and
# tryBranchInPreheader() laid a test in front from whatever arm the walk of the typed copy stood in. The loop is still bought for `given`: the row is asked whether it leaves the lists as they are
# with `extra` among them, since its read is typed on its own way, where a failing test begins the turn again in the other copy.
# f1 = inOneArm, f2 = inEveryTurn; v1 = extra. The test's VALUE may be made in front, since the loop does not change `extra`; what counts is where the BRANCH on it stands: in f1 a jump follows the test.
# OPTIONS: check=Validate
# RUN: walk f1 f2 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
# CHECK: = TypeTest v1 testedType=Array
# CHECK-NEXT: Jump ->
# CHECK-LABEL: code f2:Body
# CHECK: = TypeTest v1 testedType=Array
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch
# CHECK: isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
# RUN(SHELL): run-in-shell globalThis.sink = print;
# SHELL: 5 10 5
# SHELL: exited with 0
